  "reason": "The records collectively point toward SPS and sintering-temperature optimization for powder-derived HEAs: R3 shows that SPS of mechanically alloyed powder can produce full density, R6 and R9 connect higher sintering temperature with compaction and diffusion-enabled densification, and R11 links higher SPS temperature to improved corrosion resistance. Other records establish related roles for protective or unprotective oxide phases, passivation-layer quality, and diffusion paths. However, none identifies MgAlTiVFeCo, selects 1000 °C for that system, or predicts the specific uniformly distributed AlV2O4, FeAl2O4, and FeTiO3 phases and their combined role in chloride exclusion, parabolic oxidation, and biphasic film growth. Thus the literature suggests the general direction but not the later paper's specific intervention–mechanism combination."
